    {
      "id": "p0011-b004",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Several years ago, I started Legends of Localization, a website and a book series dedicated to explaining how popular games and movies change during the jump between languages. I've also written books about the history of bad video game translation and what happens when you try to let a computer translate an entire video game on its own.",
        "raw": "Several years ago, I started Legends of Localization, a website and a book series\ndedicated to explaining how popular games and movies change during the\njump between languages. I've also written books about the history of bad video\ngame translation and what happens when you try to let a computer translate an\nentire video game on its own.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.10369517,
          0.27250714,
          0.70877665,
          0.35863571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.0953065,
          0.27179286,
          0.71286524,
          0.35970714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          11,
          12,
          13,
          14,
          15
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "几年前，我创办了 Legends of Localization 网站和同名书系，介绍热门游戏、电影跨越语言时会发生什么变化。我还写过关于糟糕游戏翻译的历史，以及把整款游戏交给电脑自行翻译会发生什么的书。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
